research/reports/memory-retention-continuation-2026-11-01/cubic-exit-spec.md:25:Primary-source recheck, accessed 2026-11-01: [Handler et al. 2019](https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC9012144/), Results on compartmentalized cAMP and ER calcium and Discussion on brief independent versus paired stimuli; [Himmelreich et al. 2017](https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC6168074/), Results on differential receptor/G-protein dose responses; [Cohn et al. 2015](https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC4732734/), Figure 7 text/legend and Methods pairing intervals; [Berry et al. 2012](https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC4083655/), abstract, DAMB results and discussion. These support distinct signaling and the existence of active forgetting, not this equation. In particular, sensitive DAMB signaling cautions against explaining all biological forgetting by this single protected update. No figures, supplements or complete dose-response fits were inspected.
