documentation/design/research-goals/memory-handoff-2026-11-07.md:5:## 1. The memory the claims need
documentation/design/research-goals/memory-handoff-2026-11-07.md:6:
documentation/design/research-goals/memory-handoff-2026-11-07.md:7:The researcher's words: "a memory that supports learning, so that it can learn useful memories that will be stored as experience." Their later questions added three requirements: no overwriting, no clues, and memory that can feed reasoning. Together, these are four properties.
documentation/design/research-goals/memory-handoff-2026-11-07.md:8:
documentation/design/research-goals/memory-handoff-2026-11-07.md:9:| # | Property | Plain meaning | Needed for |
documentation/design/research-goals/memory-handoff-2026-11-07.md:10:|---|---|---|---|
documentation/design/research-goals/memory-handoff-2026-11-07.md:11:| Property 1 | **In the fly's own connections** | Learning changes connection strengths inside the modelled fly circuit, through a biologically justified rule driven by a teaching signal through the modelled teaching pathway (dopamine neurons). Not a separate store. | Vol. 2 |
documentation/design/research-goals/memory-handoff-2026-11-07.md:12:| Property 2 | **Lasts while the fly keeps learning** | Learn A, then learn B, then test A: A still works. Also new learning and correction still work. Measured under capacity pressure, with overwrites reported. | Vol. 2 (pass) or Vol. 4 (proven limit) |
documentation/design/research-goals/memory-handoff-2026-11-07.md:13:| Property 3 | **Helps on new positions, with no clues** | On boards from games never used in practice, choices are better than with no learning and with shuffled feedback. The fly chooses among **all legal moves**; no filter tells it that a safe answer is in the list. Feedback reaches it only through its own teaching pathway. | Vol. 2 |
documentation/design/research-goals/memory-handoff-2026-11-07.md:14:| Property 4 | **Stores lessons, not only cases** | It keeps general rules (for example "taking a defended piece is risky") that can be combined on an unfamiliar kind of position, where no similar case was stored. | Vol. 3 |
documentation/design/research-goals/memory-handoff-2026-11-07.md:15:
documentation/design/research-goals/memory-handoff-2026-11-07.md:16:**Three levels of "new"** (Property 3 versus Property 4): (1) the same board again: memorisation; (2) a new board, the same kind of situation: recall of similar cases (Property 3); (3) a new kind of situation: combining lessons (Property 4, the researcher's definition of reasoning: "being able to apply many unrelated concepts to solve an unfamiliar problem").
documentation/design/research-goals/memory-handoff-2026-11-07.md:17:
documentation/design/research-goals/memory-handoff-2026-11-07.md:18:**Allowed aids, if disclosed:** an engineered memory is allowed as a labelled computational aid for Vol. 3 (researcher, 2026-11-01, [decision log](../../../research/project/decision_log.md)). It does not count towards Property 1 or Property 2. Any reasoning result that uses it must beat a lookup-only control, so that the fly, not the store, is shown to do the work.
