documentation/design/research-goals/memory-handoff-2026-11-07.md:35:
documentation/design/research-goals/memory-handoff-2026-11-07.md:36:### 2b. The engineered store (Property 3 only)
documentation/design/research-goals/memory-handoff-2026-11-07.md:37:
documentation/design/research-goals/memory-handoff-2026-11-07.md:38:| Version | Result | What it taught |
documentation/design/research-goals/memory-handoff-2026-11-07.md:39:|---|---|---|
documentation/design/research-goals/memory-handoff-2026-11-07.md:40:| v1 | never run | design faults (oldest-match wins; wrong random control) |
documentation/design/research-goals/memory-handoff-2026-11-07.md:41:| v2 | fails | the Kenyon-cell code shrinks the deciding one-piece difference 48 times |
documentation/design/research-goals/memory-handoff-2026-11-07.md:42:| v3 | fails | ties and unequal practice decided the scores |
documentation/design/research-goals/memory-handoff-2026-11-07.md:43:| v4 | fails | raw and random keys learn; the fly's key barely does |
documentation/design/research-goals/memory-handoff-2026-11-07.md:44:| v5 | fails | a position-centred fly key helps, but more experience does not |
documentation/design/research-goals/memory-handoff-2026-11-07.md:45:| v6 | passes (audit pending) | **shortcut**: capture against quiet move; below random capture (131-145 v 250) |
documentation/design/research-goals/memory-handoff-2026-11-07.md:46:| v7 | fails (1 seed) | only about 300 relevant experiences per seed |
