29:## Measurement and integrity repairs
30:
31:Keep the original schedule. Add per-phase disk snapshots, streamed local-observation receipts, exact input codes and code hashes, true fresh-model restore (first seed), source/input identities and per-item/per-seed outcomes. Analyze the original marks separately from stricter diagnostics; do not upgrade median-of-median gates into universal success. Receipts independently replay local updates and check synthetic consequence bindings; they cannot alone independently establish the full graph's recorded neural activity.
32:
33:Resources: one sparse graph process, heap 256 MiB, RSS <=2048 MiB, free system memory >=256 MiB, duty .5, bounded elapsed 10800 s. Pace by short segments, publish progress after each arm and checkpoints before progress acknowledgments. Interruption never silently restarts work; preserve partial receipts and snapshots. New outputs only.
34:
35:Order: (1) independent old-result audit, (2) small local-math checks, (3) development run with informative/absent/matched-shuffled/disabled arms, (4) independent receipt replay and mark calculation, (5) only if joint success, specify and execute a fresh-seed delay/continued-learning test without changing the rule.

