research/reports/replay-diary-design-review-2026-11-17\design-revision-4.md:51:| `admit(lesson)` | The receipt of a lesson that delivered a pulse: `stimulus` (the input: photoreceptor indices and currents), `teaching` (dopamine group and current), `lesson_index`, `receipt_hash` | Nothing | Unknown events are refused. Any entry with the same `stimulus_hash` is removed first (correction). Then Algorithm R decides whether the lesson is kept and which entry it replaces. No field value other than `stimulus_hash` affects any decision |
research/reports/replay-diary-design-review-2026-11-17\design-revision-4.md:52:| `nextReplay(lesson_index)` | The index of the lesson just taught | One stored `(stimulus, teaching)`, chosen uniformly at random among entries from earlier lessons, or nothing if there are none | Never looks at the stimulus to choose. Never returns more than one entry. Never returns a score, count or average |
research/reports/replay-diary-design-review-2026-11-17\design-revision-4.md:61:| `stimulus` | a few thousand (index, current) pairs, about 16 KiB | Exactly what the fly's photoreceptors received for the move, including the move highlight and the dim captured piece |
